/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050636#post1050636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never claimed to. I personally took offense with the writing and the man behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050580#post1050580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No trans person has ever spoken like that. Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:11:21-08:00","id":1050642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050639#post1050639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is what I was talking about.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then I apologize for that, but I stand by my offense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:19:11-08:00","id":1050648,"title":"","content":"I'm not really going to touch what is, or is not, offensive to people. Everyone has their limits, and I am not one to say it wasn't.<br /> <br /> It didn't trip me up. The character in question did not offend me, and I was kind of fond of her, crazy as she is. I tended to like all the characters, and was sad when many of them died. <br /> <br /> Now, the setting changes, I want to touch on those....<br /> <br /> Okay, so....<br /> <br /> - Tremere were portrayed as cult-like and inhuman. They were shown as hard-liner Noddists. More Sabbat like, imo.<br /> <br /> -A mention of a Beckoning, drawing Elders east. No more info on this. <br /> <br /> -'You are what you eat' Not a fan of this, as I have said. It seems to only affect certain Disciplines, and others don't work. A character mentions Elders (like LaCroix) do not believe in it, the thinblooded thinks Elders play by the same rules. (Will VtM 5e assume Thinblood games as the base?)<br /> <br /> -The fall into inhumanity seems faster and... more accepted? There was no bemoaning lost humanity. It happened, and all the Kindred understood it as a facet. They stayed hidden, being monsters, but they never seemed to view it as a bad thing. Just a natural occurrence.<br /> <br /> - 'The Cabal', maybe a name for the Tremere, or for the Camarilla in general now?<br /> <br /> -Clans are a thing. Brujah, and Tremere are name dropped. Case's sire seemed to be a Caitiff, and an old one at that. (mentioned to be 1,000 years old, maybe hyperbole.)<br /> <br /> -Sabbat never factored into it. I assume they would exist still.... but...<br /> <br /> <br /> SPECULATION TIME<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Sabbat/Cam split doesn't exist, and only the Cabal exists now?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:48:44-08:00","id":1050662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050642#post1050642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, then I apologize for that, but I stand by my offense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I am sorry if you felt like I was talking to you like you didn't know what you were talking about. I just think it is important to acknowledge that trans people can and do say things like that.<br /> <br /> And I also wanted to say that I don't think that's shameful to do that, and from what little I know of the author (He plays D&amp;D with porn stars?) I don't think his depiction was intended to shame or stereotype transwomen. He strikes me as very sex-positive. The fact that he's cis makes zero difference to me. Anyway, I am more concerned with the story than who the author was as a person... (the author is dead. Sort of. The author is undead? The author is a vampire? Ok, enough joking around. ;p )<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;Transwomen are dishonest sluts that like to exploit cis men by luring them into sexual situations before revealing their penises because that's what they do&quot; is what the author was trying to do when he portrayed the character. I know that is a stereotype you often see in movies and comedies and the like, and it's one that is understandably upsetting to trans people. But I honestly think he was trying to be more empowering than that.<br /> <br /> Basically, what I took away from the character is that this woman has taken advantage of her vampire's curse as a way of taking revenge on the prejudiced society she lives in. Yes, she uses sex as a weapon. However, it's a dual edged sword: she puts herself above the kine, and loses a bit of her humanity in the process. Would she have done this if she weren't a vampire? Probably not. It's also kind of hard not to root for her when she gives those transphobes what they have coming.<br /> <br /> Edit: So I've done a little research on Zac and it's pretty clear he is a controversial figure... I can't make heads or tails of a lot of this stuff, with both his defenders and detractors throwing accusations of dishonesty. I am not sure where I stand on all of it, but it does look like he was banned from RPG Net for being toxic to arguments, which would seem to explain the conflict surrounding him. Ugh.<br /> <br /> I'll stand by my original position, but emphasizing that I can understand why people feel the way they do about this character. Both my perspective and Lex's perspective on the character are both valid. I can also understand how the author might turn people off from the story or even color their reading of it. I myself won't read Orson Scott Card because of things he's said, so I would be hypocritical if I criticized someone for not wanting to read Zac's work. All of this business about brigading and sock-puppeting makes discussing this really uncomfortable and I hate it. <br /> <br /> That said, I did enjoy the game, I look forward to playing Refuge, and I am really kind of excited about what White Wolf is doing with the properties from what I have seen so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":".  Looked into Zac... felt like there was more to say. 02-17-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:19:17-08:00","id":1050679,"title":"","content":"Haven't gotten but I am a little intrigued by it. If it had been a little cheaper or three of such visual novels I probably would have gotten it right away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050648#post1050648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Tremere were portrayed as cult-like and inhuman. They were shown as hard-liner Noddists. More Sabbat like, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are a cult-like pyramid and vampires in general tend to be inhuman by their very nature, especially to an outsider that is new to Kindred society.<br /> <br /> It could be the 5E is bringing back the Tremere Antitribu or taking a cue from the upcoming V20 Beckett's Jyhad Dairy, the rise of a Tremere splinter group. Or it could just be a fringe Tremere coterie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050648#post1050648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The fall into inhumanity seems faster and... more accepted? There was no bemoaning lost humanity. It happened, and all the Kindred understood it as a facet. They stayed hidden, being monsters, but they never seemed to view it as a bad thing. Just a natural occurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair this is the third VtM game and none of them have ever really done to much degree. Redemption did have a bit of that with Christof from time to time and Bloodlines pretty much skipped over that entirely.<br /> <br /> And honestly I haven't seen too many players in the TT engage in that kind of stuff for very long, mostly because they wish to engage in the rest of what VtM provides.<br /> <br /> So I don't really begrudge them for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050648#post1050648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- 'The Cabal', maybe a name for the Tremere, or for the Camarilla in general now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could just be the Tremere coterie's name for itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050648#post1050648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Clans are a thing. Brujah, and Tremere are name dropped. Case's sire seemed to be a Caitiff, and an old one at that. (mentioned to be 1,000 years old, maybe hyperbole.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they get rid of the Clans? This is still VtM. It's not like they are creating a brand new Vampire line like what WW did with VtR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050648#post1050648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Sabbat never factored into it. I assume they would exist still.... but...<br /> <br /> SPECULATION TIME<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Sabbat/Cam split doesn't exist, and only the Cabal exists now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the Sabbat didn't appear in the story doesn't mean they don't exist. Just because Case didn't encounter them doesn't mean they aren't around. I've played plenty of VtM chronicles where there was no appearance by the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Again, this is the Fifth Edition of Vampire: the Masquerade, not Vampire: the New Game. I highly doubt they are going to make such sudden and radical changes like that from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:57:06-08:00","id":1050701,"title":"","content":"They have shown they will not shy away from making sweeping changes, ala your Disciplines come from what kind of blood you have in you, and arn't, seemingly, inherent powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T15:56:12-08:00","id":1050776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1050679#post1050679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they get rid of the Clans? This is still VtM. It's not like they are creating a brand new Vampire line like what WW did with VtR.<br /> <br /> Just because the Sabbat didn't appear in the story doesn't mean they don't exist. Just because Case didn't encounter them doesn't mean they aren't around. I've played plenty of VtM chronicles where there was no appearance by the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, for me this comes off as the devs trying to keep the lore of VtM as light as possible.<br /> <br /> It's a choose your own adventure game, something far less...involved then the Bloodlines RPG. So it would make sense for this not be as lore heavy. That this is all meant as just a taste of the setting for newcomers. Which is perfectly fine in the format this story took place in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T16:07:57-08:00","id":1050779,"title":"","content":"As much as that is probably true, the possibility of certain clans and bloodlines being axed or merged is there. What we can expect from VtM 5e is a big question mark. I think it's good to state what we know exists, as a fact. So it's clear those things still exist in some form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T16:52:06-08:00","id":1050795,"title":"","content":"Could anyone played the game write about how you are what you eat actually works?<br /> <br /> If disciplines are totally based on that, what distinguishes the clans from each other mechanically (in the case that it's discernible in any measure from the story)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T16:54:46-08:00","id":1050798,"title":"","content":"There's no mechanics in the game. You can kind of see it, but there's no back end system to it. It gives you the effect. Like... in one part, you can use celerity when you run away if you had eaten someone who was filled with fear, fight or flight, when you ate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:06:42-08:00","id":1050803,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm still having serious doubts how this would work in non-confined environments like these games and theme-focused LARPS, nonetheless with the more obscure powers but we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:27:57-08:00","id":1050809,"title":"","content":"PMark, those are the same misgivings I have. If I end up liking the 5e system, I know I will end up house ruling it away, anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:20:34-08:00","id":1050848,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've got a lot of discussion about it on the Vampire forums when it started to seem this is how 5e will be.<br /> <br /> In short, I just don't think it'll solve the &quot;humans aren't important&quot; problem, while potentially adding a lot of bookkeeping and inconvenience to the game. I just see more problems with it at his point, than positive parts. But I'll reserve judgement until the final rules are came out.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we'll have more information and actual experiences after WoD Berlin. It's hard to not know anything about the plans, concepts and direction, I still think it would be better for them to do it with some kind of open development, with feedback about their ideas from the fanbase and wide playtesting. <br /> <br /> I also hope they won't make 5e an absolutely narrative-based, super rules light, diceless game, because those are just not my cup of tea. I was very excited when heard that 7th Sea 2nd ed will be a thing, then the rules completely made me uninterested. I hope it won't happen again with my favorite games and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T21:00:15-08:00","id":1050872,"title":"","content":"This would be the offensive bit. One of them - the part about the severed ass is pretty eye-rolly too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/5yEiIi5.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img 