included a Ventrue MRA that uses Dominate to find definite victims of rape, rape them himself, and then used Dominate to force them to tell the police that they faked their report of the real rape that happened against them. How would this make you feel?<br /> <br /> How would you feel if people went, &amp;quot;MRAs don't care about this MRA character, they care about Zak's anti-MRA politics.&amp;quot; And yes, Zak is very anti-MRA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope. This is not acceptable.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Dracula isn't a book with really problematic racism in it, because it's fiction and vampires aren't real!&amp;quot; is not how things work.<br /> <br /> Bigotry being promoted by fiction is bigotry by the authors, not make believe just because the story is fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div> This wasn't me defending Zak, at minimum he seems needlessly abrasive without an ounce of diplomacy, so you could be absolutely right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:18:50-08:00","id":1053183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1052959#post1052959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this kind of amusing considering that Zak has very strong views about objectification that would probably make you ideological opponents in any discussion of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not a &amp;quot;horny trans character&amp;quot; it's a &amp;quot;serial killer trans character that kills anyone that doesn't meet her ideological purity test.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's a pretty big difference there. If you're not progressive enough in her eyes, she kills you. That might not be an attack on the LGBTQ community, but it is piss poor representation of LGTBQ individuals in fiction.<br /> <br /> In an effort to try to put this into context you'll identify with. If the story included a Ventrue MRA that uses Dominate to find definite victims of rape, rape them himself, and then used Dominate to force them to tell the police that they faked their report of the real rape that happened against them. How would this make you feel?<br /> <br /> How would you feel if people went, &amp;quot;MRAs don't care about this MRA character, they care aboutstory s anti-MRA politics.&amp;quot; And yes, Zak is very anti-MRA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope. This is not acceptable.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Dracula isn't a book with really problematic racism in it, because it's fiction and vampires aren't real!&amp;quot; is not how things work.<br /> <br /> Bigotry being promoted by fiction is bigotry by the authors, not make believe just because the story is fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div> I get what you mean, I know countless MRAs who would flip out, I'm not one of them, I made myself the main villain in it, a perverted mutant who did all kinds of evil things, including rape (it was fictional and hyper unrealistic, in RL I'm a chill pussy cat, I wrote the story in exchange for free porn). This was long before I became an MRA, long before I even had heard of MRAs. <br /> <br /> That was the story in which I created Trinity, my in character daughter who had 3 brains each with it's own personality. <br /> <br /> The original brain was Sydney, a Canadian who who was the most rational brain, with the power of Telekensis. Then each of her breasts developed it's own brain with super powers. <br /> <br /> The right breast brain was called Macy, she was American and had the power of Pyrokenisis, and the left brain breast was Rebecca, she was French with Cyrokenisis, and Macy and Rebecca didn't get along at all with Sydney having to play peace maker between them. It lead to some embarrassing situations. <br /> <br /> I miss my Trinity character, she was cool. <br /> <br /> Anyways I'm not a normal MRA by any stretch of the imagination, most would be enraged and hurt by the scenerio you put out, so I get you're point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:27:42-08:00","id":1053267,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Zak intended the serial killer trans character to be a manifestation of his own political fantasy about killing those who he considers to be regressives, transphobics, Trump voters. <br /> <br /> Yes the character is trans, but it's not unheard of for even CIS writers and roleplayers to create stand ins for facets of themselves that are of a different gender, sex, even race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:31:09-08:00","id":1053423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1053183#post1053183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..I made myself the main villain in it, a perverted mutant who did all kinds of evil things,..</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your point. I think there's a few differences though.<br /> <br /> First, you made a character based on yourself. Whether you believe the character in this game is a snipe at a game design Zak has gone after, or Zak's co-author, this is not the case here. The character, according to the co-author is based on trans porn actress Bailey Jay. Making a character explicitly based on other people means readers are going to read into this fact.<br /> <br /> Second, what you're making the character for matters. Writing your character wasn't for a professionally publish piece of fiction for a less over the top setting. What we make for our own personal games (or for other people since you said it was a trade) only needs to meet the standards of a few private individuals. If I make an offensive piece of trash character that never makes it out of my notebook... so what? If I try to make money off selling a story with that character? That's a different kettle of fish.<br /> <br /> Third, you're not trying to create controversy with a character. WW's latest official blog post has made it clear that they want this character to push buttons. If your goal is to piss off transphobes by shoving awesome trans characters into your creative output, you need to avoid sabotaging the goal by making a character that reinforces transphobic stereotypes and offends trans people instead.<br /> <br /> Again, going to an MRA example. If you were writing an MRA character that's supposed to push the buttons of anti-MRA people, would you make a character that fits all the anti-MRA tropes and makes MRAs look bad, or would you make an MRA character that challenges all those tropes by playing on them but subverting them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1053267#post1053267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Zak intended the serial killer trans character to be a manifestation of his own political fantasy about killing those who he considers to be regressives, transphobics, Trump voters.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the public statements from the creators involved... this doesn't seem to be the case. The best guess intention I can infer from their direct statements are that they wanted to created an awesome transwoman vampire that would make people that get upset at diversity and inclusion in stories riled up and look stupid for being upset by an awesome character.<br /> <br /> So... I think we can agree that if that was the goal... the Avery character is pretty much fail. Trans readers aren't feeling awesome about this character, and anti-representation Internet ranters actually have reasons to point at this character serving minimal purpose but to shove trans characters in their faces.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:16:52-08:00","id":1054003,"title":"","content":"What in the hell is MRA","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:26:17-08:00","id":1054008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1052841#post1052841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you know what else is unrealistic, and actually imposdible instead of merely being improbable? Fucking Vampires and a secret society of vampires!</div> </div> </div> </div> 1. Don't buy Camarilla lies.<br /> 2. It just seems like a poor way to survive. Killing every Uber driver who supports Trump? Just seems like a lot of murder adding up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054003#post1054003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What in the hell is MRA</div> </div> </div> </div>Men's rights activist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:25:26-08:00","id":1054045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054008#post1054008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. It just seems like a poor way to survive. Killing every Uber driver who supports Trump? Just seems like a lot of murder adding up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare it to <s>Zack's self-insert</s> the guy with green mohawk who goes around slaughtering police precincts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054003#post1054003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What in the hell is MRA</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly - a male mirror to feminism, both positive (advocating for men's rights, research into male-only diseases and so on) and negative (misogynists). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> undoubtedly refers to the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:45:08-08:00","id":1054054,"title":"","content":"My personal feelings on MRAs and the MRM (Men's Rights Movement) are not positive but, I'm referring to the general concept because it's a political identifier Omegaphallic uses for himself. I'm bringing up the negative stereotypes of MRAs solely to illustrate the negative stereotypes Avery represents to many LGBTQ people (specifically the idea that non-heterosexual cisgender individuals are really trying to attack &quot;normal&quot; people instead of fighting for their right to exist equally with other people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:21:24-08:00","id":1054099,"title":"","content":"I really wanted it to be good, and it was pretty good for a while, but that one exchange with Avery pretty much soured the whole experience for me.<br /> Hearing that the character might be based on a trans game dev named Avery that the author has beef with makes me regret my purchase. I sincerely hope that all future endeavours from White Wolf deal with their subject matter more respectfuly.<br /> <br /> Just tried the Mage one too, I thought it was a lot better, really liked the fact that it didn't railroad you as hard as the Vampire one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:07:14-08:00","id":1054219,"title":"","content":"Us older players may remember back in the day there was this thing called WoD: Gypsies. It was a learning experience for the old WWGS. This controversy is a bit like that, but I dont think anyone involved in WoD:G was ever intending to insult anyone, so maybe its different. It seems to me though that it's all just little bits of history repeating...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:17:18-08:00","id":1054220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1053089#post1053089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither of these do anything but make the character more problematic. She's a liar (remember Zak S abhors liars), or she's a serial sexual assaulter/murderer, or a mixture of these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a liar and/or a serial killer. Sounds like a creature wholly unsuited for a vampire game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:51:59-08:00","id":1054230,"title":"","content":"Well, besides the fact that a serial killer in VtM is supposed to be horrible for your Humanity (she's on the fast track to Humanity 2 at best), why the hell does an immortal monster give a shit about killing humans over their petty political beliefs? If she's a liar, it's not some grand political vampire trickery. She's just lying to some neonate to make herself look dangerous/awesome at getting all men to let her suck them off.<br /> <br /> And this is a character that, &quot;...positively broadens the range of transgender portrayal in games,&quot; because she's, &quot;kick-ass&quot; and is nice to the main character. It's rather hard to reconcile how the official White Wolf blog characterizes her narrative and artistic purpose, with the actions she's portrayed as doing. She's supposed to be a character that makes prospective trans players say, &quot;that's awesome, this is a game that I can seem myself in, and thus want to play!&quot; by having the most prominent trans character wax on about how awesome it is to kill people on the flimsy pretense that they're probably not pro-LGBTQ enough.<br /> <br /> If you want to see a character that positively broadens the range of transgender portrayal in games by being kick-ass, look no further than the cover of Exalted 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T10:51:03-08:00","id":1054373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054230#post1054230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why the hell does an immortal monster give a shit about killing humans over their petty political beliefs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without really stepping into the discussion, that one has such a simple answer:<br /> <br /> Because she finally can.<br /> <br /> I don't want to imagine what some people would do if they were suddenly in a position to murder, and actually knowing they can get away with it.<br /> Also, as a twist of irony, I think somebody on the path of humanity is MORE bound to do this than those on the more monstrous paths..because those monsters really don't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:43:56-08:00","id":1054420,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of human killers out there. If someone wants to stalk Uber drivers to find targets to kill... you don't need to be a vampire to do it.<br /> <br /> I can certainly emphasize with a story about any character becoming a vampire and in exploring their new nature, kills some stand-ins for all the bad people that tormented them. But that's not what Avery's doing. She's past that point. She's past, &quot;I'm a vampire bad ass and I'm going to get some righteous vengeance!&quot; stage, and is supposed to be at the point of getting over that shit because it will just drag her down into the clutches of the Beast. She knows she's not making a difference. She knows she's not carefully stalking bad people.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, &quot;she can.&quot; But that's not really the point. The point is her role in the story and the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:29:05-08:00","id":1054481,"title":"","content":"There's one question that, unless I misse it, hasn't been asked yet that I feel needs to be: Who are these Preludes for? <br /> <br /> They were marketed to be introductions to the world of Masquerade and Ascension for new players who've never heard of the setting before, and if so then what themes were gone over in the Preludes? How exactly did they sell VtM and MtAs? Taking all of the design decisions in the best possible light even, or at least the most liberal benefit of the doubt, what exactly was told by these stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-24-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:34:28-08:00","id":1054593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054420#post1054420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's plenty of human killers out there. If someone wants to stalk Uber drivers to find targets to kill... you don't need to be a vampire to do it.<br /> <br /> I can certainly emphasize with a story about any character becoming a vampire and in exploring their new nature, kills some stand-ins for all the bad people that tormented them. But that's not what Avery's doing. She's past that point. She's past, &quot;I'm a vampire bad ass and I'm going to get some righteous vengeance!&quot; stage, and is supposed to be at the point of getting over that shit because it will just drag her down into the clutches of the Beast. She knows she's not making a difference. She knows she's not carefully stalking bad people.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, &quot;she can.&quot; But that's not really the point. The point is her role in the story and the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>i read a theory in 4chan that the avery is basically a stand in for some types of posters either here on RPG.net. In the same vein that Avery sets a moral bar and if you fail to meet it she kills you is like when someone says things like &quot;this clan/tribe/tradition is offensive and should be removed and if you disagree with it you are a racist/bigoted/homophobe&quot;<br /> <br /> And the more i think about it with Zak\u00b4s issue with RPG.net i dont see it that far fetch.<br /> <br /> I so far i have only played the Ascension game and i didn't like its portrayal of the technocracy. My main issue is that i dont see the technocracy taking that particular side on the whole argument of immigration issue. The problem with using RL issue in wod is that sometimes the faction existing in the setting is gonna either ignore the issue or make its less about the issue itself.<br /> <br /> Example: I could see the technocracy being in favor of the immigration but at the same time using the influx of scared refugees to set centers of educations to purge them of their &quot;dangerous &quot;practices and beliefs&quot;&quot;, which was a line from the technocrat you encounter. With the traditions being split on the issue, with the local mages being concerned that the influx of other ethnicities is gonna push them culturally aside.<br /> <br /> Instead the leftist leanings of the author made the pro immigration the &quot;good side&quot; and the anti immigration the &quot;bad side&quot; and obviously the traditions would be on the &quot;good side&quot; and the technocracy on the &quot;bad side&quot;. Maybe a case could be made that the country was a syndicate economic experiment and that the refugee just upset that experiment but it wasn't never addressed that way.<br /> <br /> So my problem with Dracula\u00b4s approach to RL issues is that the factions in WoD as written dont necessarily gonna be clear cuts stands ins for the sides of the RL issue. Or that the will do things around the RL issue without specifically intervening diluting or relegating the RL issue to the background. Dracula\u00b4s approach seems to just overwrite the faction in favor of the RL issue when to me the Faction is always above the RL issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-24-2017, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:57:10-08:00","id":1054606,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure about that. The defense of Avery is that she's supposed to be a positive character; that's she's not an attack on RL people, but a promotion of someone you want to be like.<br /> <br /> Zak's public statements regarding how to treat people he disagrees with lines up just as much as Avery being a bit of a fulfillment of his revenge fantasies. He is a man that's publicly said that the majority of people being right-handed is a divine sign of our need to punch people that hold right-wing political views. I'm sure he wasn't being entirely literal, but he is extremely prone to using violent (literal violent, not hurtful) language when discussing conservative/right-wing proponents even if he's careful to avoid direct incitement.<br /> <br /> I mean, neither option is good. If you take Martin, Zak, and Sarah at their word, the character is violent revenge fantasy wish-fulfillment.<br /> <br /> If you don't buy their statements, then it's hard not to see it as a pathetic snipe at people over minor disagreements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:38:23-08:00","id":1054637,"title":"","content":"Real life current politics should not be used in WoD for this reason. Rage across the World used the Arab Spring as a backdrop, but didn't involve the characters in it directly. Avery killing Trump supporters is very VERY close to some mentalities I have seen on tumblr, put to the extreme by actually doing it. And it sets a bit of an...unfortunate image of these people. Especially as she is trans on top of it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:09:19-08:00","id":1055243,"title":"","content":"What I wonder though is what this is a prelude <i>to</i>. That 5th edition stuff that's on the horizon?<br /> <br /> Also, going by the screenshots the interface is several flavors of atrocious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:44:14-08:00","id":1055288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055243#post1055243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I wonder though is what this is a prelude <i>to</i>. That 5th edition stuff that's on the horizon?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a sort of way to attract new players, personally. Prelude to the real VtM gaming and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:57:30-08:00","id":1055377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055288#post1055288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is a sort of way to attract new players, personally. Prelude to the real VtM gaming and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what a wonderful introduction! Hammy, jilted dialogue which wouldn't fit into fanfiction in places, along with the whole Avery thing. Blergh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:36:46-08:00","id":1055392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055377#post1055377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what a wonderful introduction! Hammy, jilted dialogue which wouldn't fit into fanfiction in places, along with the whole Avery thing. Blergh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets worse, since what Avery does is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gay_panic_defense#Trans_panic\" target=\"_blank\">actually legit deadly</a> to actual trans people. So not only is it badly written, it also makes mockery of issues actual trans people face.<br /> <br /> Given the MET werewolf, and the whole edgy try plus adding IRL current issues extremely clumsily (check out Children of Revolution and Rage across the World how to do it right), it seems like a massive downgrade from the content Onyx Path has put out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:32:27-08:00","id":1055444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055392#post1055392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it seems like a massive downgrade from the content Onyx Path has put out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of Onyx Path WoD releases have been great. Which is why I hope that the new WW looks to Onyx Path devs when creating the new books.<br /> <br /> Eddy Webb, Gentleman Gamer, Justin Achilli, and Stew Wilson all do great, great stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:39:21-08:00","id":1055445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055392#post1055392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It gets worse, since what Avery does is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gay_panic_defense#Trans_panic\" target=\"_blank\">actually legit deadly</a> to actual trans people. So not only is it badly written, it also makes mockery of issues actual trans people face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any chance of him getting un-paid, all of the stuff in the app getting un-written, and someone worth their salt writing a decent story? Maybe one where the trans characters aren't ideological set-pieces designed to undermine 'that person I don't like' and 'those people I don't like'. I mean ideally trans characters would be apolitical, they'd just be the same as a character with detached or attached earlobes, but we are DEFINITELY not in that world. A trans character is a political statement, and that statement HAS to be validating if it's going to avoid hurting people. Are you allowed to write trash which hurts trans people? Sure! Does anyone have to read it, pay for it or respect your writing? No. Free speech goes both ways. And I certainly won't cry if the backlash spills over into the writer's wider life. I've seen similar cases where people have contacted other employers and placed pressure on them to get a reaction, and while I would never join in I have never shed any tears.<br /> <br /> We're reaching the point where a character being gay can just be because they're gay, it isn't political, and there are few places you can't go. My players feel comfortable with the Harpy's childe being a hyper-sexualised pervert because they know that isn't a political message I'm trying to spread, there are plenty of sexually conservative or prudish gay characters and they're comfortable with the idea that I'm not calling myself and them perverted weirdos. With transgender people it's different. Nuanced storytelling on that front takes time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:42:57-08:00","id":1055446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054220#post1054220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a liar and/or a serial killer. Sounds like a creature wholly unsuited for a vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, up next for my PCs is the greedy Jewish Ventrue Prince Karl Goldhoarder. Greediness and stealing are perfectly vampiric traits, so it isn't a racist caricature at all!<br /> <br /> As a side note, when do people start thinking I'm an edgy dude? It looks like fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T04:36:58-08:00","id":1055593,"title":"","content":"And fixing Avery wouldn't even be that hard. Keep her status as a prostitute, take away the uber thing, tone down the sexualization and bragging and make her kill those who try to kill her out of trans panic. There you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:22:35-08:00","id":1055699,"title":"","content":"I apologise for this tangent, but<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1052959#post1052959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dracula isn't a book with really problematic racism in it, because it's fiction and vampires aren't real!&quot; is not how things work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what is missing in that statement is &quot;in the context of its time&quot;. Sure, we can all agree, that by the standards of 2017, Dracula's depiction of gypsies and hungarians (or hungarian gypsies, twas a while ago that I read it) is not particularly positive, but in the context of its own time, it wasn't anything particularly incendiary. Hell, British Gothic fiction is basically built on the trope of everything not british being old and decadent and corrupt (whereas everything british is old, glorious, and pure).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1052959#post1052959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bigotry being promoted by fiction is bigotry by the authors, not make believe just because the story is fiction.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a rather hardline stance to take, and robs the author of any and all agency (because it pushes all interpretative agency onto the reader). Or, to quote the (admittedly, right-leaning) author of the Drakaverse:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>&quot;T<b>here</b> is a technical <b>term for someone who confuses</b> the opinions of a character in a book with those of the author. That <b>term</b></b><b> is idiot.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> (I do not mean to imply you are an idiot, its just a nice, and to-the-point quote)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit 2: All that said, yes, this Avery character seems ridiculously over-the-top, and a walking Masquerade breach waiting to happen. Peppering her dialogue with a few comments on how fickle humans are, toning down the Trump thing (wth, honestly), and making her sexually aggressive (as in &quot;as opposed to the usually sexually more passive portrayal of women&quot;) without going waaaay over the top, and presto, she is merely irritating.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 02-27-2017, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:20:09-08:00","id":1055732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055446#post1055446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, up next for my PCs is the greedy Jewish Ventrue Prince Karl Goldhoarder.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what the Ventrue Antitribu actually believe the mainline Ventrue to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:23:26-08:00","id":1055758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055732#post1055732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what the Ventrue Antitribu actually believe the mainline Ventrue to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Antitribu are Dirty Larpers, so who's really winning ;-) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:32:50-08:00","id":1055765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055699#post1055699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what is missing in that statement is &quot;in the context of its time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really... It doesn't matter that it wasn't incendiary. The book has problematic treatment of racism in it. That doesn't change of the context of when it was written. The context of when it was written only impacts how we should look at the text in terms of appreciating art with problematic elements in it.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm fine being a fan of the novel Dracula because the racist elements are a product of the times.&quot; is fine with me. &quot;I'm fine being a fan of the novel Dracula because it isn't racist because at the time people didn't consider that stuff racist.&quot; is not fine with me.<br /> <br /> I'm even less of a fine of the idea that the novel being about a vampire excuses any problematic depictions in it. Dracula being a story about how immigrants are out to steal our women does not go away just because Dracula is a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, we can all agree, that by the standards of 2017, Dracula's depiction of gypsies and hungarians (or hungarian gypsies, twas a while ago that I read it) is not particularly positive, but in the context of its own time, it wasn't anything particularly incendiary. </div> </div> </div>There's two very different things there.<br /> <br /> The book's depiction of Hungarians is pretty much non-existent beyond Dracula not liking them (which is completely in character because the Hungarians of the time were political enemies of the Wallachians).<br /> <br /> The book's depiction of the Szgany/Rom is completely different as they're portrayed as Dracula's servants and get massacred for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is a rather hardline stance to take, and robs the author of any and all agency (because it pushes all interpretative agency onto the reader). </div> </div> </div>It might be hardline, but it does nothing to rob the author of agency. A novel can't &quot;promote&quot; bigotry without the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [FONT=arial]<b>&quot;T<b>here</b> is a technical <b>term for someone who confuses</b> the opinions of a character in a book with those of the author. That <b>term</b></b><b> is idiot.&quot;</b> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with this. But I don't think I've committed this mistake either. I've been careful to ensure when I'm talking about which and how they interact with each other. In the case of Zak and Avery though, there's a lot of evidence to support the idea that she is a character who's opinions are designed to express the opinions of the author. Zak has said things that amount to, if it weren't illegal, we should all punch people for having right-wing ideologies. And he wrote a character that kills such people because she feels she can get away with it.<br /> <br /> Confusing the author and the character, is a lot more defensible when there's a strong case for a character being the author's mouth-piece.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:28:19-08:00","id":1055898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055699#post1055699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=arial]<b>&amp;quot;T<b>here</b> is a technical <b>term for someone who confuses</b> the opinions of a character in a book with those of the author. That <b>term</b></b><b> is idiot.&amp;quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This quote ignores the nuances of storytelling. Stories are political. They take sides, by and large. My Anarch game is consciously anti-conservative, framing austerity as a move by the Ventrue Methesulahs to siphon resources to prepare for Gehenna. That's a good allegory for austerity, but it is most certainly political, and I confront that because I'm a mature storyteller.<br /> <br /> Pretending media isn't political flies in the face of critical theory and the very nature of media. The writing presents a Message about transgender people. It's written so that the character's vilest aspects are codified to be connected to her trans status. It doesn't take a genius literary critic to see the agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:21:48-08:00","id":1055930,"title":"","content":"If anyone wanted my perspective, everything in the entire world is political, and as the writer of a fictional world chooses literally every aspect of that world, our fictional worlds are political too.<br /> <br /> If my main character has red hair, I chose to give her red hair, because I created literally everything in my world, from nothing. Maybe it's because I have red hair and I'm making my character a particular self-insert--side point, literally every character a writer creates is a self-insert to one degree or another. Maybe it's because there's some symbolism behind red hair in the world I've created. Maybe it's because I want her to stand out and I recognize that red hair is the rarest hair color. There is still a reason for every single thing I specify. I might not even recognize the reason. But as I am a human, not a robot, and humans are, by our very nature, political, every choice I make in my texts is a choice and is subject to your analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:31:46-08:00","id":1056008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1054481#post1054481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one question that, unless I misse it, hasn't been asked yet that I feel needs to be: Who are these Preludes for?<br /> <br /> They were marketed to be introductions to the world of Masquerade and Ascension for new players who've never heard of the setting before, and if so then what themes were gone over in the Preludes? How exactly did they sell VtM and MtAs? Taking all of the design decisions in the best possible light even, or at least the most liberal benefit of the doubt, what exactly was told by these stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>...since no one seems to want to answer this, I will. Especially since I still consider myself a relative newcomer to the WoD setting.<br /> <br /> Both stories, at their core, maintain the central story arc that a beginning player character would face in the VtM and MtAs settings. The VtM one being about needing to adjust and adapt to your new life as a nocturnal monster and all the awful things they would have to do because of it. The MtAs on how there's a war of belief and it concerns people who have the literal Will to make their beliefs reality, and how a beginning PC needs to decide which side they fall on said war. These would be the kind of things that would come up a lot in your typical VtM or MtAs game.<br /> <br /> Strip everything away with the central story and I personally think it was successful on that end...<br /> <br /> The issue is, of course, everything else. In this case, the framing of the narrative.<br /> <br /> VtM it's the execution of the narrative...and is something already been discussed way too much here and that I won't get into. For MtAs it's framing the narrative around the refugee crisis in Europe and the Middle East.<br /> <br /> The thing about bringing &quot;politics&quot; with these products is how...absolute they are. That they portray their &quot;politics&quot; as: &quot;This is the way how things are, and should be. Anything else to the contrary of what I say is inherently WRONG. And there is nothing you can say or do that can prove otherwise&quot;. Which, in a piece of interactive fiction like these Preludes, is a big turn-off.<br /> <br /> You are essentially forcing a viewpoint on the player(s). Whether they like or not. In the VtM Prelude, this is an issue with the game design in the last section of the game. In the MtAs Prelude, it's by declaring that only one perception of the refugee crisis is the correct choice. And any other choice is the wrong choice, and always will be.<br /> <br /> Although what's confusing to me is that this is nuWW's first notable product release. And with the subtitle of &quot;Prelude&quot; it makes you think that there's going to be more after this...but, isn't the Werewolf video game nuWW's only major digital product on the horizon? If so, why isn't there a WtA Prelude?<br /> <br /> And it's endlessly amusing to me that Mage was one of the first digital products by nuWW since for me, Mage is the least suitable property to be made into a video game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:55:34-08:00","id":1056024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1055898#post1055898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This quote ignores the nuances of storytelling. Stories are political. They take sides, by and large. My Anarch game is consciously anti-conservative, framing austerity as a move by the Ventrue Methesulahs to siphon resources to prepare for Gehenna. That's a good allegory for austerity, but it is most certainly political, and I confront that because I'm a mature storyteller.<br /> <br /> Pretending media isn't political flies in the face of critical theory and the very nature of media. The writing presents a Message about transgender people. It's written so that the character's vilest aspects are codified to be connected to her trans status. It doesn't take a genius literary critic to see the agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll gladly grant you that everything is political (and at no point did I, or Stirling, claim otherwise, so please take your horse and lance to another windmill). I'll even gladly grant you that in this specific case, we are dealing with an endorsement of bigotry, or at the very least, a biased and heavy-handed representation.<br /> <br /> What I will not, categorically, grant, is that in all cases, representation equals endorsement. In this case, it surely does, but writing about bigotry, hell even writing about bigotry in a way that in the universe of the work, seems promotional, does not mean the writer endorses bigotry, which was the phrase I took umbrage with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:13:30-08:00","id":1056036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056024#post1056024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll gladly grant you that everything is political (and at no point did I, or Stirling, claim otherwise, so please take your horse and lance to another windmill). I'll even gladly grant you that in this specific case, we are dealing with an endorsement of bigotry, or at the very least, a biased and heavy-handed representation.<br /> <br /> What I will not, categorically, grant, is that in all cases, representation equals endorsement. In this case, it surely does, but writing about bigotry, hell even writing about bigotry in a way that in the universe of the work, seems promotional, does not mean the writer endorses bigotry, which was the phrase I took umbrage with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally representation of views isn't the same as endorsing them. One thing I loved about Night Siege (I think that was the one) was how the Camarilla used Racial Profiling via the Police Force to win wars against the Sabbat, since their neonate intake in the US is very high in black and latino youths. That's a nuanced representation of how a group of evil Vampiric bastards can use bigotry to their advantage, and I was impressed by it. It feels very real, and it doesn't feel like an endorsement of bigotry because it absolutely isn't.<br /> <br /> While I can't give you a technical definition of where Representation of Bigotry becomes Promotion of Bigotry (I think there is a distinct and obvious difference, but it's difficult to effectively define), I think it's important that we're critical of works which don't care for the former and dive right into the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:12:55-08:00","id":1056314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056024#post1056024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I will not, categorically, grant, is that in all cases, representation equals endorsement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's actually saying this is the case though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056036#post1056036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can't give you a technical definition of where Representation of Bigotry becomes Promotion of Bigotry (I think there is a distinct and obvious difference, but it's difficult to effectively define), I think it's important that we're critical of works which don't care for the former and dive right into the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not technical, I would generally set the line at the point where the author/creator treats bigotry as a positive aspect of a character.<br /> <br /> For example, Magneto is an incredibly sympathetic character. You completely understand how Magento came to be the man he is, and I think a lot of people would struggle to say they would definitely avoid the same path. But his bigotry against normal humans is still what makes him a villain. His unwillingness to accept that humans and mutants can learn to live in harmony and thus humans need to go is written as a bad thing no matter how much you can relate to him (or how much the good guys manage to being assholes/hypocrites in their own ways).<br /> <br /> Going back to Dracula, Van Helsing's casual bigotry is portrayed as a completely beneficial aspect of his efforts to fight a monster. His willingness to slaughter minorities to get at the vampire ruling over them is written as a good way to approach the problem. It's not even a moral compromise. It's treated like it's a side bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:43:16-08:00","id":1056409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056314#post1056314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going back to Dracula, Van Helsing's casual bigotry is portrayed as a completely beneficial aspect of his efforts to fight a monster. His willingness to slaughter minorities to get at the vampire ruling over them is written as a good way to approach the problem. It's not even a moral compromise. It's treated like it's a side bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I read Dracula many times. I'm from Eastern Europe. Sorry, I can't agree with that. It's absolutely not in the focus of the book. Dracula had servants, who happened to be gypsies and the hunters killed a few to get to him, because they defended Dracula. Wouldn't it been as bad if those servants haven't been gypsies, but Romanians or Hungarians? That's double standards.<br /> <br /> Yes the connection between gypsies and the evil vampire <i>could</i> be seen as playing into the &quot;racist stereotypes&quot; surrounding gypsies, but, especially at that time that was a cultural element of our region and Europe in general. <br /> <br /> That's the thing I just can't stand behind, despite my fairly liberal worldview, the notion that everything is about racism/sexism etc. That's forcing everything into a certain narrative, when history, cultures and such are much more complex. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:54:33-08:00","id":1056453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056409#post1056409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's absolutely not in the focus of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It not being the focus of the book (which is a much more racist message about how evil immigrants are, and that's not really any modern making up of themes, it's just modern people thinking that it's a bad message). I'm talking about characters that represent bigotry vs characters that promote bigotry. It being a minor point in the story doesn't change that Van Helsing is entirely too OK with killing minorities (Dracula has plenty of servants are not minorities and Van Helsing is all about saving them from Dracula's grasp).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dracula had servants, who happened to be gypsies and the hunters killed a few to get to him, because they defended Dracula. </div> </div> </div>A bunch of guys with repeating rifles gun down a group of people who's most advanced weapons are knives, when the text goes out of the way to repeatedly show that they'll run away in fear from rich men with guns willing to shoot people. The text never shows that the heroes were in any threat from Dracula's non-vampire servants of any ethnicity, but the Syzgany are the only ones that get killed instead of freed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't it been as bad if those servants haven't been gypsies, but Romanians or Hungarians? </div> </div> </div>Well, the other group were Slavs, but yes, if Van Helsing was all for killing Slavs and ignoring the Syzgany would also be racist in the context of the story where Dracula's mortal servants are repeatedly shown to not be threats or desire to die for their ruler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the thing I just can't stand behind, despite my fairly liberal worldview, the notion that everything is about racism/sexism etc. </div> </div> </div>Everything is still political, as addressed above.<br /> <br /> If you don't like my example, whatever, I don't feel it gets away from the point being made. &quot;Not everything is about racism,&quot; doesn't mean these two examples aren't validly about racism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:06:40-08:00","id":1056792,"title":"","content":"Ok, I re-read the end of the book itself, because I wasn't sure that the hunters actually killed any gypsies in the book ( I remembered that there was a firefight in the Coppola-movie) and rightly so, because no, they didn't. The gypsies sported knives <i>and </i>pistols and aggressively defended D, they didn't shown any inclination to run away &quot;from the rich men with guns&quot;. The hunters called for surrender repeatedly but didn't shoot anyone. Van Helsing didn't shoot anyone. There was no slaughter of innocent gypsies by the Triumphant White Men. When the hunters pushed through the gypsies to D, Mr. Morris got stabbed and that was all the blood spilled. So, I'm sorry in fact the scene you based your interpretation wasn't in the book. I'm not 100% sure, but I think the only ones killed in the whole book by the hunters were only the vampire brides, Lucy and D. <br /> <br /> As for how much Dracula is about &quot;immigrants steal our women&quot;, I have serious troubles with that, because the fact that Dracula was Eastern European didn't get the fraction of focus in comparison to the fact that he was a vampire. The Carpathian origin was more or less just an exotic place on the edge of the modern world where ancient horrors could still walk the night. In a sense that is a distinctively Imperial thought, but I won't call it downright racist. I don't say that the fear from immigrants didn't influence Stoker, because it certainly did to some extent, but it's not the focus of the book in my eyes and certainly not some nefarious underlying message.<br /> <br /> As for Stoker's picturing of Carpathian ethnicities, as a local, I'd say he didn't do it in an overly negative way (honestly he didn't do it in much length, it was more showed as exotic curiosity for tourists) and get it mostly quite close to reality (and reality isn't nice every time, so a not entirely flattering portrayal of any group is okay to me).<br /> <br /> <br /> For closing it, I want to address the &quot;everything is political&quot; notion. We won't agree on that, but I figure it's worth saying that in my eyes that's a quite lopsided view. Yes, every author is and was influenced from the surrounding socio-political environment, his/her upbringing, etc. but that's not the same as everything having a political message or statement as a goal. In fact, it says more about the consumer side to me if one sees political messages in everything and looks at everything through the lens of political worldview and forcing everything into that framework. It's somewhat like how Marx simplified history into the struggle of classes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:53:12-08:00","id":1056850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056453#post1056453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like my example, whatever, I don't feel it gets away from the point being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to repeat myself directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T21:39:44-08:00","id":1056973,"title":"","content":"Then what's the thrust of your point? If I run a game with an antagonist who espouses fascist ideals I'm secretly a fascist pushing a hidden agenda? Characters within fiction are not hidden messages of what the writer truly feels. Ever read a book with a serial killer character, do you think the author is a serial killer? I mean Stephen King aside, in Darly Dreaming Dexter Jeff Lindsay portrays the title character sympathetically, so he's pro serial killing vigilantes?<br /> <br /> Edit: this isn't support for Zak, nuWW or the Avery character, just a response to the bizarre rhetoric that all fiction is somehow a reflection of what the writer feels or desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 03-02-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T23:03:24-08:00","id":1056996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056973#post1056973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what's the thrust of your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Authors that treat [bad real world things] as <b>positive</b> aspects of a character are promoting those things.<br /> <br /> If your fascist character's fascism is treated as a negative trait, you're saying fascism is bad. If your character's fascism is treated as a positive trait, you're saying fascism is good.<br /> <br /> Not really sure how that's complicated; or really that controversial.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are some situations where things can be &quot;informed&quot; traits where the author says &quot;fascism is bad, and is a character flaw for this character,&quot; without the fascism the character espouses ever having negative consequences, but that's a matter of execution over the difference between representation vs. promotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I run a game with an antagonist who espouses fascist ideals I'm secretly a fascist pushing a hidden agenda? </div> </div> </div>Promotion isn't the same as &quot;secretly pushing a hidden agenda.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, the answer to this question is more complicated. Antagonist vs. not antagonist is not the point. Those are narrative roles in the story. Antagonists can represent/promote positive traits (we tend to call these sympathetic and compelling villains because they have positive traits we can identify with as whatever their negative traits are that override those positive aspects).<br /> <br /> How you treat the espousal of fascist ideals is what matters to whether or not you're promoting fascism. Is the character an antagonist because of their fascism detracts from what you think are better ideals, or is the fascist part being treated as effectively good but the character is bad for some other reason? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Characters within fiction are not hidden messages of what the writer truly feels. </div> </div> </div>Generally because they're not hidden.<br /> <br /> Characters are not all representations of the authors. However characters are always representations of the author's feelings. You can't write a character that doesn't reflect your personal perspective, because every character you write is a creation of your personal perspective.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean writing a fascist character makes you a fascist. It means how you write that character is going to reveal things about your personal perspective about fascism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ever read a book with a serial killer character, do you think the author is a serial killer? </div> </div> </div>It is exceedingly taxing on my ability to treat your posts charitably to actually think you're asking this in good faith.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how many times I have to repeat things, but this should be abundantly obviously not what I'm saying in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean Stephen King aside, in Darly Dreaming Dexter Jeff Lindsay portrays the title character sympathetically, so he's pro serial killing vigilantes? </div> </div> </div>Even just sticking to the early material, the books are attempting to address a far deeper question than this: if someone's a serial killer, can they attempt to follow an ethical standard to channel their urges?<br /> <br /> Lindsay is arguing that if you have to kill (esp. considering the later books and the source of Dexter's urges), you should try to put that to a societal good by being a vigilante that goes after proven evil doers instead of risking your urges being let out on the innocent. But the setup of the character is important here. Dexter <b>has</b> to kill. He doesn't have a choice. His choice his who he's going to kill. You can argue different moral positions (such as just killing yourself), but it's a much more nuanced issue Lindsay explores than, &quot;Dexter is a serial killer vigilante, so he's saying you should be one too!&quot;<br /> <br /> Lindsay also had some reason for wanting to explore the central question of the Dexter series. I have no idea. But you don't just do that for no reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...just a response to the bizarre rhetoric that all fiction is somehow a reflection of what the writer feels or desires. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how this is so strange. The only issue I see is that those of us advocating that this is the case are being misrepresented as meaning this is always endorsement by the writer (esp. after posts trying to show the differences between representing things vs. promoting them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T03:50:55-08:00","id":1057041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056996#post1056996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how this is so strange. The only issue I see is that those of us advocating that this is the case are being misrepresented as meaning this is always endorsement by the writer (esp. after posts trying to show the differences between representing things vs. promoting them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as especially seen by your reading of Dracula, in many cases it boils down to &quot;I can read this and this into the work, therefore it not only <b>is</b> there, but it <b>was put there by the author&quot;</b>. (the first one being that from your modern reading, this can be interpreted as such, and the second one being authorial intent). One only needs to read something from an old, or different culture to see how this is completely and blatantly false. You can read issues into lets say Romeo and Juliet (a relatively modern work) that simply did not exist back then, apart from very broad strokes.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that critical theory, when applied with proper academic rigour, is not useful. But what I object to is the <b>blatant projection of one's own interpretation into a work, and then accepting that interpretation as not only valid, but correct as far as the author is concerned</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056996#post1056996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lindsay also had some reason for wanting to explore the central question of the Dexter series. I have no idea. But you don't just do that for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be true, but lets not assume we know the reason, and lets especially not make moral, or moralistic judgements based on whatever reason we assume. It might be something as simple as &quot;this is interesting because it is not the norm&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1056996#post1056996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Authors that treat [bad real world things] as <b>positive</b> aspects of a character are promoting those things.<br /> <br /> If your fascist character's fascism is treated as a negative trait, you're saying fascism is bad. If your character's fascism is treated as a positive trait, you're saying fascism is good.<br /> <br /> Not really sure how that's complicated; or really that controversial.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right. Is Starship Troopers (pick a version) fascist?<br /> <br /> There is not a single in-universe frame of the movie, that in universe, treats fascism as bad. Yet to say it is promoting fascism would be missing the point by a mile.<br /> <br /> Is Dune fascist? Is God Emperor of Dune fascist, with its very positive portrayal of Leto Atreides II (he is ultimately proven right)? If so, is Frank Herbert a fascist?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>In-universe positivity is not the same as out-of-universe positivity.</b> Verisimilitude is a thing, and you are fundamentally asking a work of fiction to break that, to the detriment of that work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps we should take this into the OT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 03-02-2017, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T06:42:48-08:00","id":1057067,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5238_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5238\" data-vbnamecard=\"5238\">Herbert_West</a> THANK YOU. I could not have expressed it better. People seem to equate their own perceptions, biases, analyses, projections with author's intent, and are all too eager to label any and all works of art and fiction as problematic, racist, sexist, transphobic, promoting wrong-think etc. Perhaps it isn't the artist, but the reaction of the beholder, that should be analyzed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:52:10-08:00","id":1057111,"title":"","content":"The term 'wrong-think' gives me the shivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:25:19-08:00","id":1057288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057041#post1057041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, as especially seen by your reading of Dracula, in many cases it boils down to &quot;I can read this and this into the work, therefore it not only <b>is</b> there, but it <b>was put there by the author&quot;</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... so it's OK to misrepresent what someone's saying because you disagree with their example's validity?<br /> <br /> Your argument right now is, &quot;Heavy Arms reads too much racism into Dracula, so lie about what he's saying to make him look bad.&quot; That doesn't seem like a really productive stance.<br /> <br /> And yes, it was put there by the author, because the author put it there. Dracula contains what it does, because the author put it in there. If you disagree with my analysis of it, whatever, but please stop acting like purposefully misrepresenting my statements is a reasoned disagreement with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One only needs to read something from an old, or different culture to see how this is completely and blatantly false. </div> </div> </div>How does reading old stuff prove that misrepresenting my points is false? I mean, I'm glad that you're acknowledging that what you're saying is actually blatantly false, but this is nonsensical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can read issues into lets say Romeo and Juliet (a relatively modern work) that simply did not exist back then, apart from very broad strokes. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't demonstrate anything about what I said. It's just a meaningless generality.<br /> <br /> And there's not much to read into Romeo and Juliet. The point of the story is in the introduction: Blood feuds between rich families are dumb, and result in stupid teenagers doing stupid teenager stuff in a context were people are killing each other... and it ends in them dying instead of listening to the reasonable adults in their lives. It's not a subtle story.<br /> <br /> Most of stuff that gets read into the story has nothing to do with the context of the time it was written in, but people forgetting that it's not supposed to be a story about the ultimate love of two people for each other. People have been treating it as way more romantic than it was meant to be for a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not to say that critical theory, when applied with proper academic rigour, is not useful. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I'm not going to not use critical theory in a casual conversation because you want to insist on a hypocritical standard of academic rigor as a means of shutting me up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what I object to is the <b>blatant projection of one's own interpretation into a work, and then accepting that interpretation as not only valid, but correct as far as the author is concerned</b>. </div> </div> </div>So... you object to people applying critical theory and thinking that they're right when they reach a conclusion that's different than yours?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Might be true, but lets not assume we know the reason, and lets especially not make moral, or moralistic judgements based on whatever reason we assume. </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there.<br /> <br /> Despite 100% agreeing with what I said, you added, &quot;lets especially not make moral, or moralistic judgements based on whatever reason we assume.&quot; to <b>blatantly fucking lie</b> about me having done so, without having to show that I did!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All right. Is Starship Troopers (pick a version) fascist? </div> </div> </div>Books: No, but it struggles with the depictions of fascism and the author attempted to correct this in expanded material (which is usually ignored in discussions of it). The story attempts to explore the concept of earned franchise vs. inherent franchise (at least regarding to big political things) and uses a militaristic fascist society to create a situation where the two can be at odds with each other. The text somewhat gets distracted from picking a side on this as it gets into the psychological cost of earning citizenship/franchise via military service, though the expanded work that highlights that non-military service is a path towards franchise and without the Bugs external threat the fascist elements of that society grow significantly weaker. The stories essentially make the case that an earned franchise society at war will tend towards fascism, without answering if that tendency is worth it compared to issues with inherent franchise society.<br /> <br /> Movies: A complete mess of different creative agendas with no clear voice. Between the floundering attempts to satirize the book's difficulty in addressing fascism in some places, and losing the pro-soldier anti-military dynamic of the book for a military action movie instead (and basically what all the sequels focus on), the movies end up incoherent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is not a single in-universe frame of the movie, that in universe, treats fascism as bad. Yet to say it is promoting fascism would be missing the point by a mile. </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Dune fascist? Is God Emperor of Dune fascist, with its very positive portrayal of Leto Atreides II (he is ultimately proven right)? </div> </div> </div>No. Besides the fact that Dune isn't actually about fascism (there are more forms of authoritarianism...), but Paul and Leto II directly state that the tyranny of their rule is a bad that they consider a necessary evil. Leto II wholly acknowledges that he should be considered a monster that's perpetuated the greatest evils that generations upon generations of humans will ever know, because he feels (and is right) that being a tyrant is what humanity needs to escape the trap of precognition, and without escaping it they will never survive to the looming threat beyond it.<br /> <br /> The Dune series is very clear that Paul and Leto II are also forced into their roles and are trapped in them against what they believe to be moral/ethical. Paul has things thrust on him, but tries to find a different path and fails. Leto II has to do what his father wouldn't do because there is not third option for them because of their power is a trap.<br /> <br /> The Dune series is very clear that it's against the concentration of power in the hands of the elite, because it says that power is a trap that perpetuates humans into a state that is incapable of the adaptability they will need to survive as a species. Paul and Leto II are not heroes because they're tyrants. They're heroes because they set forth on a path to destroy the system that created them to ensure no human gains that much power ever again, and humans become decentralized enough to endure any future catastrophe. Which gets down right anarchistic, if on a very large scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>In-universe positivity is not the same as out-of-universe positivity.</b> </div> </div> </div>I know everyone seems to have enjoyed not quoting it, but you did read my whole Magento example, right? Where the in-universe presentation of Magneto is frequently positive towards his motivations, without crossing the line into out-of-universe promotion of race wars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Verisimilitude is a thing, and you are fundamentally asking a work of fiction to break that, to the detriment of that work. </div> </div> </div>I haven't asked a work of fiction to do anything. I've said that works of fiction shouldn't get a pass on their content for being fiction.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking for a book set in the US south before the end of slavery to not have slavers, or only portray rich whites as evil people. I saying that a character arguing that slavery is good for black people to not be treated as an out-of-universe good person in any new fiction, and in old fiction that we recognize that as racist bullshit instead of trying to excuse it because some people actually thought that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057067#post1057067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem to equate their own perceptions, biases, analyses, projections with author's intent, and are all too eager to label any and all works of art and fiction as problematic, racist, sexist, transphobic, promoting wrong-think etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, how dare people think critically about what the media the consume. But of course, I doubt you recognize how silly it is to argue about people projecting about an author's motivations, as you project your perceptions about those peoples' intent yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps it isn't the artist, but the reaction of the beholder, that should be analyzed. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it should be both. Holding artists accountable for their work doesn't exclude holding reviews accountable for their work while we're at it.<br /> <br /> So... how about you start. Why are you and Herbert here so dead set on railing on casual critical analysis of literature that finds a piece of art to be problematic? What's the appropriate analysis of this reaction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057111#post1057111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term 'wrong-think' gives me the shivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that's the point. To make critical analysis the same as censorship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:37:52-08:00","id":1057330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057041#post1057041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because, as especially seen by your reading of Dracula, in many cases it boils down to &quot;I can read this and this into the work, therefore it not only <b>is</b> there, but it <b>was put there by the author&quot;</b>. (the first one being that from your modern reading, this can be interpreted as such, and the second one being authorial intent).</div> </div> </div> </div>It especially gets problematic, when the accusation was based on something that's not even in the book, like in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:05:46-08:00","id":1057416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057288#post1057288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how about you start. Why are you and Herbert here so dead set on railing on casual critical analysis of literature that finds a piece of art to be problematic? What's the appropriate analysis of this reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe general problem I have with applying critical theory to everything is that it's a fast way to confirmation bias. If you sit down with a book and say &quot;Today I'm going to read <i>Dracula </i>\u200bwhilst looking for racism&quot; then <i>of course </i>you're going to find racism. Every interaction in the book will be skewed in a way that confirms the bias that the reader applied going into reading the book. The critic is going into the work having already made up his or her mind about what the conclusion of the analysis is going to be, and is now looking for bits to cherry pick that fits this conclusion, instead of going in cold. There's nothing wrong with wanting to study the author's intent behind a work of fiction, but going in with a preconceived notions about the author's intent is more likely than not going to lead to an unfair interpretation of the work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:07:51-08:00","id":1057439,"title":"","content":"I would also like to add that that post of mine from when I entered the conversation was needlessly confrontational. While I think critical theory has its inherent problems, I could have gone about expressing it in a more civil fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:47:59-08:00","id":1057450,"title":"","content":"For what it is worth, as someone who is about to get a chapter published about vampires including literary analyses of Dracula, the idea that it doesn't touch on race is...a shallow reading. Dracula is pretty explicitly a foreigner and the narrative is about rejecting and ejecting the rapacious, greedy, vile predator foreigner who has invaded Britain. <br /> <br /> That is a really really basic and common interpretation of the text. It has more history than the damn games we are talking about. I am so very confused that noticing this and commenting on it is something something censorship wrongthink whatever. <br /> <br /> There are multiple readings of the text, but Dracula as a foreigner who physically invades the shores of England and needs to be repelled by a motley groupd of good Brits and her allies is neither reaching, nor unfair. Linking it to concerns of the era about Eastern Europeans and immigration is pretty damn solid. Sure, Stoker doesn't spoon feed you this stuff but it isn't exactly a subtle narrative.<br /> <br /> (Authorial intent is a tricky beast but we are all shaped by our communities and cultures and media, so when we just so happen to replicate them in our own work, deliberate or not, they still stand as ideas invoked by our work and occasionally complicit in wider forms of oppression)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:49:07-08:00","id":1057451,"title":"","content":"Also, nobody goes in cold to a narrative. Ever. But even moreso in the case of classics with as much impact on genre and media as Dracula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T22:10:34-08:00","id":1057459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057416#post1057416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe general problem I have with applying critical theory to everything is that it's a fast way to confirmation bias.</div> </div> </div> </div>But your still assuming intent. How do you tell the difference between someone that sat down for an as cold as possible reading of Dracula and finds it has some racist elements in it, and someone that went looking for racism and found the same thing? Is that even a problem?<br /> <br /> Your response is still that people doing casual critical theory analysis of literature and art are all doing it to find a problem, instead of doing it for any other reason. Why is there an assumption of intentional bias?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T17:01:51-08:00","id":1057837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057416#post1057416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you sit down with a book and say &quot;Today I'm going to read <i>Dracula </i>\u200bwhilst looking for racism&quot; then <i>of course </i>you're going to find racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go further and say, if you approach the book with the firm notion that the people of the 19th century (and/or British people were that especially) were racist and xenophobe, you'll find those concepts in nearly every book written in that time period, because you're trying to apply modern sensibilities backward.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying those people weren't racist and xenophobe in comparison to progressive liberal concepts of nowadays, because they were. I just say, a given work is not a work about racism, just because the cultural environment is so in comparison to nowadays. Stoker for example, didn't showed neither minorities, nor Eastern Europe culture in an unfairly, or condescending way, to prove the superiority of white Englishmen in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057450#post1057450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it is worth, as someone who is about to get a chapter published about vampires including literary analyses of Dracula, the idea that it doesn't touch on race is...a shallow reading. Dracula is pretty explicitly a foreigner and the narrative is about rejecting and ejecting the rapacious, greedy, vile predator foreigner who has invaded Britain.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a thing as over-analyzing a text. That way you'll get Harry Potter, which is really about mental disorder and derangement and the horrors of boarding schools, or Lord of the Rings, which is a World War analogy. Not necessarily untrue in a sense that the authors were naturally influenced by different things, but those are not what the books are about and not the story in them.<br /> <br /> The Victorian British fear of immigrants might played into Stoker's choosing of D's birthplace, but I doubt he wrote his book with the intent of &quot;Ahhaa! I'll write a book about evil foreigners and cleverly disguise it as a vampire story!&quot;. And I won't even call it racism, since D is a white European nobleman.<br /> <br /> To close my argument with an anecdote: here, in Hungary, one of our biggest writers (incidentally also from the 19th century), J\u00e1nos Arany answered to a question regarding his most famous work &quot;I don't remember how or what I thought.&quot; Sometimes a story is just a story and the cultural background of the writer, while interesting and important to look at, is not necessarily the focus of the story and not every story is an intentional comment on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:36:38-08:00","id":1057886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057837#post1057837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go further and say, if you approach the book with the firm notion that the people of the 19th century (and/or British people were that especially) were racist and xenophobe, you'll find those concepts in nearly every book written in that time period, because you're trying to apply modern sensibilities backward.</div> </div> </div> </div>This still has the same issue of, &quot;I'm allowed to say your analysis is incorrect because I can assert you are biased/ill-intentioned without having to back it up.&quot;<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stoker for example, didn't showed neither minorities, nor Eastern Europe culture in an unfairly, or condescending way, to prove the superiority of white Englishmen in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't disprove any points made. It's just a different set of opinions made my another modern person with biases that may or may not have impacted this analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's a thing as over-analyzing a text. That way you'll get Harry Potter, which is really about mental disorder and derangement and the horrors of boarding schools, or Lord of the Rings, which is a World War analogy. Not necessarily untrue in a sense that the authors were naturally influenced by different things, but those are not what the books are about and not the story in them. </div> </div> </div>And yet... Tolkien's own grandson advocates that the LotRs might not be about WWI told as a fantasy story, but it is absolutely about the horrors and damages - to both individuals and cultures - of the industrialization of warfare that Tolkien experienced in WWI.<br /> <br /> &quot;Over analyzing&quot; might be a thing, but it exists on a spectrum. Saying the LotR is a story about WWI might be on the end of the spectrum, but saying that WWI is not part of the LotR at all then gets to be clearly on the &quot;under analyzing&quot; part of the spectrum as it completely rejects the clear elements shaped directly by Tolkien's experiences in WWI. Something like WWI is a giant conceptual thing, and a piece of literature can absolutely include parts of that thing without trying to be about all of that thing. LotR isn't about the politics that created the atmosphere for WWI, or taking sides in the war (there heroes are not the Allies, the enemies are not the German alliance), but it is about how society changed irreversibly by the brutality of large scale industrial warfare<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Victorian British fear of immigrants might played into Stoker's choosing of D's birthplace, but I doubt he wrote his book with the intent of &quot;Ahhaa! I'll write a book about evil foreigners and cleverly disguise it as a vampire story!&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Stoker left plenty of notes about his research into the story, and it paints a picture that's more the other way around. &quot;I want to write a vampire story, but I need a conflict that will get my English readers to care about my research into vampire mythology, oh, I'll have my vampire come to England as an evil foreigner!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I won't even call it racism, since D is a white European nobleman. </div> </div> </div>Now who's applying modern sensibilities backwards? 19th century racism did not hold all &quot;white&quot; Europeans as an equal race. Esp. in late 19th century racism (aka when Dracula was published), there was a growth of a strain of racism in Europe that conflated nationalism with racism. Late 19th century racism wouldn't consider a British man and a Romanian man the same race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and not every story is an intentional comment on that. </div> </div> </div>Just because it wasn't intentional doesn't mean it isn't worth analytical examination. Unintentional problematic elements of the story are still valuable to acknowledge as such for the sake of how we chose to experience those stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:53:27-08:00","id":1057897,"title":"","content":"It doesn't matter if we do it intentionally. It's still there. I don't understand why this is so difficult to grasp. We are people. We have biases. We have life experiences. They shape our art, whether we intend it or not. Intent is irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:53:52-08:00","id":1057942,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to say there is no subtext or authorial intent, I was negatively reacting to character ideals or presentation of an idea automatically assigning those attributes and beliefs to an author. If there is a racist character in my game, even if he's an ally of the player characters, doesn't represent my rascist tendencies, even if I don't go out of my way to portray the character in a negative way. I'm probably just being lazy and assigning a noticible trait, even if it's a negative trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:10:10-08:00","id":1058028,"title":"","content":"Literally no one here is saying that the presentation of an idea automatically means one can assign that idea to the author.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:50:32-08:00","id":1058160,"title":"","content":"I came the closet to saying that, but even then I was careful to only speak of actions rather than assigning intent or belief.<br /> <br /> To give a personal example, on a different part of the Internet, I called someone's post a &quot;word salad.&quot; Which isn't particularly nice, but to me, that was just a reference to writing poetry/lyrics in a nonsensical fashion but that fulfills a pleasing cadence or rhythm or rhyming scheme; a way to say, &quot;what you're saying sounds good but doesn't actually make sense if you look at the specifics.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, &quot;word salad&quot; is also used as a term for the psychological/neurological symptom of disordered speech. I did not realize or intent to offend the person by making them feel like I was picking on them over that, but I did. It was an act of ablism I committed via text. I don't think of myself as ablist, I hope other people don't see me that way, but in the moment I said something cruel. As a human attempting to be decent in general, it's on me to own that to make up for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:00:50-08:00","id":1058201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1057067#post1057067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5238_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5238\" data-vbnamecard=\"5238\">Herbert_West</a> THANK YOU. I could not have expressed it better. People seem to equate their own perceptions, biases, analyses, projections with author's intent, and are all too eager to label any and all works of art and fiction as problematic, racist, sexist, transphobic, promoting wrong-think etc. Perhaps it isn't the artist, but the reaction of the beholder, that should be analyzed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This 'argument' is &quot;NO U&quot; dressed up in its Sunday Best. Can we ever 100% know the Author's intent? Not really, we can construct a solid argument for their intent (for example we can all agree that the intent of Mein Kampf was to promote Hitler's image and the National Socialist platform, even though we can't prove that beyond all doubt since even expressed intent can be dishonest). But can we ever know anyone's intent, really? We need to make judgement calls, and we won't always agree. I might say that work X has racist undertones, and that author's intent is to promote a racist agenda. Someone else might agree that the work is racist, but the creator has no conscious bias and they are just repeating racist tropes. Neither of us are provably right or wrong, we're two people with different opinions on a work.<br /> <br /> I believe that you can make a solid argument for the author of this work having created Avery to fulfill some hateful fantasy against an IRL trans woman he dislikes, and inadvertently (or maybe even deliberately) spread his transphobic views to readers. Can you prove that? Well, short of a signed confession, not really. Looking at the righteous indignation towards Avery and similar depictions and saying &quot;lol you all need to calm down you're just seeing things that aren't even there, in fact maybe you're the one who's messed up&quot; isn't an argument, it's exploiting the existence of Doubt (something that no sensible person denies) and expanding on that doubt to try and shoehorn in a Rational Middle Ground <sup>TM</sup> which just comes across as general anxiety towards critical analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-04-2017, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T21:39:51-08:00","id":1058290,"title":"","content":"Let's be fair. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"348\" data-vbnamecard=\"348\">InfernalGoose</a> apologized for the tone of that post, there's no need to get to worked up about it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T02:33:15-08:00","id":1058333,"title":"","content":"I should stay away from posting when I'm in a bad mood. It doesn't do me or anyone else any favors.<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear though, I'm not writing this post whilst in a bad mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:59:42-08:00","id":1058435,"title":"","content":"I need to learn Twine and just write a 'choose your own adventure' for WtA. Or maybe a crossover. But I'm too lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:57:41-08:00","id":1058450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1058435#post1058435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to learn Twine and just write a 'choose your own adventure' for WtA. Or maybe a crossover. But I'm too lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twine! That's it. I'd love to do a WoD story in Twine collaboratively with some other writers. Set up a Master Story and then split the writing between like 5 different people (with choices near the beginning and throughout putting you in totally different situations, rather than the usual &quot;choose your own&quot; crap where you're railroaded), then have 1 writer run through everything and quality check to give it all the same Feel.<br /> <br /> Maybe start as a Mortal at one of the Sabbat's games, where they put Mortals in an underground area and chase them through (Rat Race?). Potential outcomes include dying, becoming a Hunter, becoming a Ghoul, being Embraced (by three different potential sires)... the same events unfold, but you're on different aspects of those events and your choices actually affect the outcomes quite significantly. And it wouldn't be one of those games where choosing the thing the writer doesn't want you to choose kills you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:43:11-08:00","id":1058555,"title":"","content":"The most difficult part about learning Twine is figuring out how to fit in the graphics. Once you have that down all you need to do is write.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:05:27-08:00","id":1058779,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've been fiddling around with writing a short story using Twine myself (even though things have stalled a bit). Right now it's a story that's inspired by stuff from Beast the Primordial.<br /> <br /> Little bit intimidated by the graphical stuff especially if I want to make this thing look pretty. But I'll figure things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T00:19:47-08:00","id":1058807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1058779#post1058779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I've been fiddling around with writing a short story using Twine myself (even though things have stalled a bit). Right now it's a story that's inspired by stuff from Beast the Primordial.<br /> <br /> Little bit intimidated by the graphical stuff especially if I want to make this thing look pretty. But I'll figure things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait.<br /> <br /> WAIT.<br /> <br /> People actually <i>play</i> Beast? I was under the impression that Beast was one of those nWoD games which didn't actually end up forming any sort of sizable or longlasting community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:46:40-08:00","id":1058989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1058807#post1058807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.<br /> <br /> WAIT.<br /> <br /> People actually <i>play</i> Beast? I was under the impression that Beast was one of those nWoD games which didn't actually end up forming any sort of sizable or longlasting community.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;inspired by&quot; is the key here. While Beast misses a good number of steps I do think it has merit as an antagonist splat, a bit like Mumm: The Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:20:47-08:00","id":1059159,"title":"","content":"People do actually play Beast. I have a feeling that Beast games tend to be less, &quot;less play this and only thing for a few years,&quot; vs. &quot;Lets play this for a few months between other things,&quot; kind of thing. Which is fine, not every game needs to have hardcore fans that consider it their &quot;primary&quot; game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:38:37-08:00","id":1059168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1058807#post1058807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> WAIT.<br /> <br /> People actually <i>play</i> Beast? I was under the impression that Beast was one of those nWoD games which didn't actually end up forming any sort of sizable or longlasting community.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wanted to like Beast so bad. When it was announced, I was giddy with excitement. And then after all the changes were made, I found myself less excited and withdrew my Kickstarter support. <br /> <br /> Too bad, really. It had a ton of potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:50:01-08:00","id":1059177,"title":"","content":"I think I have a bias against nWoD. It feels very... odd to me. Like I feel it's SUPPOSED to be the Majora's Mask to oWoD's Ocarina of Time, but it ends up feeling more like Faces of Evil <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:03:30-08:00","id":1059225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059159#post1059159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People do actually play Beast. I have a feeling that Beast games tend to be less, &quot;less play this and only thing for a few years,&quot; vs. &quot;Lets play this for a few months between other things,&quot; kind of thing. Which is fine, not every game needs to have hardcore fans that consider it their &quot;primary&quot; game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh, if I am not still playing it in 20 years, I am not gonna waste my time :P<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, I treat Wraith that way. In small doses the odd ghost story is quite fun. Long term... it not only gets crushingly dreary, but it is easy to lose focus on what makes ghost stories so compelling and fun in the first place.<br /> <br /> Sabbat shovelhead/siege games are good too for the odd 'limited run' game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-06-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:41:58-08:00","id":1059243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1058807#post1058807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> WAIT.<br /> <br /> People actually <i>play</i> Beast? I was under the impression that Beast was one of those nWoD games which didn't actually end up forming any sort of sizable or longlasting community.</div> </div> </div> </div>A single glance at the CoD thread will show that is not at all the case with Beast...<br /> <br /> ...no, that honor belongs to Geist the Sin-Eaters for not forming any sizeable or long-standing community!!!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, with Beast things go a bit like this: it has a lot of interesting ideas to it, but where it falls down and turns people away is because of how those ideas were explained and framed (funny enough, kind of like the main issue with these Preludes). It gets tricky, especially when people really start adhering the RAW interpretation, but I think the line has potential.<br /> <br /> It's either that or wait for the massive fix that is Beast 2nd edition years later...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:54:59-08:00","id":1059249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059243#post1059243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A single glance at the CoD thread will show that is not at all the case with Beast...<br /> <br /> ...no, that honor belongs to Geist the Sin-Eaters for not forming any sizeable or long-standing community!!!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, with Beast things go a bit like this: it has a lot of interesting ideas to it, but where it falls down and turns people away is because of how those ideas were explained and framed (funny enough, kind of like the main issue with these Preludes). It gets tricky, especially when people really start adhering the RAW interpretation, but I think the line has potential.<br /> <br /> It's either that or wait for the massive fix that is Beast 2nd edition years later...</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I LOVE the writing of Geist, but I just can't imagine playing it. Ooh, these Boneyard rules are cool... now I'm trying to imagine ACTUALLY making a boneyard &quot;IRL&quot; and I can't really picture it. Vampire works because we kind of understand Vampires, same for the other splats. &quot;Splat X, the all new Splat&quot; is a recipe for a mixed reception. Yes, Geist is a new take on Ghosts and Beast is based on real-world myths, but the simper the first page (the introduction to V20 is a great example) the simper it is to pick up fans. Don't get me started on the Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:03:57-08:00","id":1059411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059249#post1059249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I LOVE the writing of Geist, but I just can't imagine playing it. Ooh, these Boneyard rules are cool... now I'm trying to imagine ACTUALLY making a boneyard &quot;IRL&quot; and I can't really picture it. Vampire works because we kind of understand Vampires, same for the other splats. &quot;Splat X, the all new Splat&quot; is a recipe for a mixed reception. Yes, Geist is a new take on Ghosts and Beast is based on real-world myths, but the simper the first page (the introduction to V20 is a great example) the simper it is to pick up fans. Don't get me started on the Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you think about it the Manifestations of Geist aren't all that strange knowing what ghosts can do:<br /> <br /> - Boneyard: Make an area spooky.<br /> - Caul: Make a person spooky.<br /> - Curse: Curse a person.<br /> - Marionette: Possess a person.<br /> - Oracle: Spooky senses.<br /> - Rage: Lash out at a person with spooky powers.<br /> - Shroud: Give a person a spooky aura.<br /> <br /> I concede the point on Promethean however. For some I see the connection with alchemy and the humours and stuff, but for the rest? Not really.<br /> <br /> I am really looking forward to Deviant, however. It's less about traditional monsters and more about some more modern things. Though come to think of it, from what I've read you can build a pseudo-Promethean in that system. Go with low-key Variations, a not-too-powerful enemy (mommy created you and now mommy wants you back, so she hired a few people to help her) and you're kind of set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:53:46-08:00","id":1059549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059249#post1059249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I LOVE the writing of Geist, but I just can't imagine playing it. Ooh, these Boneyard rules are cool... now I'm trying to imagine ACTUALLY making a boneyard &quot;IRL&quot; and I can't really picture it. Vampire works because we kind of understand Vampires, same for the other splats. &quot;Splat X, the all new Splat&quot; is a recipe for a mixed reception. Yes, Geist is a new take on Ghosts and Beast is based on real-world myths, but the simper the first page (the introduction to V20 is a great example) the simper it is to pick up fans. Don't get me started on the Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist is absolutely not a new take on Ghosts. Geist is the rehash of &quot;Supernatural entity merged with person&quot; thing that some WoD writers have been beating to death since oWoD. Mage is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. Mummy 3e is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. Demon the Fallen is about being the supernatural entity merged with a person. Exalted is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. It's the same damned concept every time with a new color of paint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:33:41-08:00","id":1059671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059549#post1059549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a WoD game, and not actually an entity, since Exaltations don't have an independent existence in even the most theoretical capacity. They exist solely to give a reason for why humans can be so lowly yet rise to such great heights in that particular setting, not unlike being a Kryptionian, having Batwillpower, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-07-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:04:38-08:00","id":1059700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059549#post1059549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist is absolutely not a new take on Ghosts. Geist is the rehash of &quot;Supernatural entity merged with person&quot; thing that some WoD writers have been beating to death since oWoD. Mage is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. Mummy 3e is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. Demon the Fallen is about being the supernatural entity merged with a person. Exalted is about getting powers from a supernatural entity merged with you. It's the same damned concept every time with a new color of paint.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great way to immerse people in the supernatural however. You were normal, until one day you weren't. All supernaturals are like this to at least SOME degree. Wraiths have the Shadow, Vampires have the Beast, Werewolves have their War Beasts and their Spirit Side, Mages have their Avatars (as you say). Is it lazy? Maybe. IMO Vampire hits the perfect balance by having a Huge but Hidden society, and mid-life recruitment into it. Mage does a similar thing (I still struggle to imagine the Traditions/Technocracy being the majority, since most would Awaken as Orphans and stay that way in my opinion), as does Werewolf (to varying degrees and with lesser efficacy IMO).<br /> <br /> In some games I read it all and go... okay... where does the Group come in? You need a unifying society of some form or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T23:08:47-08:00","id":1059959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059700#post1059700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage does a similar thing (I still struggle to imagine the Traditions/Technocracy being the majority, since most would Awaken as Orphans and stay that way in my opinion)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as an aside, remember that Mages have the ability to see into the future (and the past), read minds, and detect Magick itself. Moreover, you have two major factions that have every reason to want to use those powers and others to find as many new recruits as possible. That's not even getting into the fact that some Mages use Entropy to manipulate their own fate, so that their Avatars will eventually reincarnate into someone who will be found by the same group they were in previously. Or the fact that both Traditionalists and Technocrats have all the best Primers, which can increase the likelihood the Awakening of any random individual they show it to (the Society of Ether basically gives a copy of the Kitab Al-Alacir to anyone who seems promising, just to see what happens). Or that, in addition to their magical surveillance, Mages on both sides (but especially the Technocracy) cultivate contacts and allies across the world, so it makes it easier to find out about strange, unexplained supernatural goings-on.<br /> <br /> In light of all that, I'm surprised <i>so many</i> Orphans slip through the cracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-08-2017, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:28:40-08:00","id":1060069,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this has been posted already, but <a href=\"https://blog.white-wolf.com/2017/02/22/breathing-the-same-shadow/\" target=\"_blank\">nuWW has weighed in on the subject of ZackS and Avery</a>. TL;DR on Zack: they retract their previous claim of not finding anything controversial about him and promise to keep his behavior in check. I find this to be rather strange since ZackS is a freelancer and nuWW can just say that they are not responsible for anything he does when not on the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The criticized character, Avery, is perhaps the most helpful and kick-ass vampire in the game. She saves your ass and is (spoiler alert!) one of two main allies at the conclusion. Like Horrocks and Sabbath, <b>we believe this character positively broadens the range of transgender portrayal in games</b>. Naturally, she will not be the last transgender character in a White Wolf game, as we continue work with designers, writers and artists from a wide range of backgrounds. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 03-08-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:01:40-08:00","id":1060088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1060069#post1060069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this has been posted already, but <a href=\"https://blog.white-wolf.com/2017/02/22/breathing-the-same-shadow/\" target=\"_blank\">nuWW has weighed in on the subject of ZackS and Avery</a>. TL;DR on Zack: they retract their previous claim of not finding anything controversial about him and promise to keep his behavior in check. I find this to be rather strange since ZackS is a freelancer and nuWW can just say that they are not responsible for anything he does when not on the job.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We saw that days ago. Since then, Zak has been caught impersonating an RPG.net mod on Reddit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T13:46:39-08:00","id":1060258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1060088#post1060088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We saw that days ago. Since then, Zak has been caught impersonating an RPG.net mod on Reddit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait.................. what? Why did he do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:11:11-08:00","id":1060275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1060258#post1060258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait.................. what? Why did he do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You ask why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/davidahilljr/posts/10155076151936204?match=YSBwbGF5IGluIHRocmVlIGFjdHMsZGF2aWQgaGlsbCx0aHJlZSxkYXZpZCx6YWsgcyxhY3RzLHBsYXksaGlsbCx6YWs%3D\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/rsrc.php/y8/r/dF5SId3UHWd.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/davidahilljr/posts/10155076151936204?match=YSBwbGF5IGluIHRocmVlIGFjdHMsZGF2aWQgaGlsbCx0aHJlZSxkYXZpZCx6YWsgcyxhY3RzLHBsYXksaGlsbCx6YWs%3D\" target=\"_blank\"> Log into Facebook </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/davidahilljr/posts/10155076151936204?match=YSBwbGF5IGluIHRocmVlIGFjdHMsZGF2aWQgaGlsbCx0aHJlZSxkYXZpZCx6YWsgcyxhY3RzLHBsYXksaGlsbCx6YWs%3D\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/davidahilljr/posts/10155076151936204?match=YSBwbGF5IGluIHRocmVlIGFjdHMsZGF2aWQgaGlsbCx0aHJlZSxkYXZpZCx6YWsgcyxhY3RzLHBsYXksaGlsbCx6YWs%3D </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:25:12-08:00","id":1060279,"title":"","content":"Also, five days after WW posted their &quot;Zak's promised to behave&quot; nonsense, Zak posted his &quot;The Cost of being Creative, The Cost of Lying,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> This a blog post that includes the following:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">A lot of the attacks on people like [removed other people references] me presume that the internet controversies we were involved in are somehow failures of professionalism or decorum\u2014mistakes, brand-damaging eruptions of resentment, lashing-out, rants, screeds penned against better judgment.</span> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">In fact, they\u2019re nothing of the sort. I am proud of every stand I ever took and I suspect so are they.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> So, keep in mind that he's not just some guy that has anger issues. Every nasty thing he's posted was a purposeful and intentional act; including all the low blows in the blog post.<br /> <br /> And his post &quot;Zak agreed to behave&quot; tirade has a number of barbs aimed at David Hill Jr., Fred Hicks, and all his traditional favored targets where he somehow made the RPG better by being an ass to people instead of making it worse by just making everything more toxic. He also dismisses all criticism about various works as being from acceptable targets to him. He never acknowledges the trans gamers that didn't like Avery, or the feminists that found <i>Kingdom Death</i> to be exploitation. Acknowledging that people that are harmed by the stuff he wants to defend would require acknowledging that he's a cishet white dude railing against other cishet white dudes while ignoring what minority voices have to say. <br /> <br /> He also takes a giant pot shot at the entire RPG industry by saying, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Before people started taking a stand, basically nothing good was getting published.&quot; which in context means that nothing good was published between 2010 and... OD&amp;D I guess (he never really does specify that one). 30+ years of people seriously working on making good RPGs (even if you don't like them as your style), and also working for pushing the boundaries of inclusivity, representation, and content? He wants all the credit for that because he came in after the RPG bubble collapse and indie RPG explosion due to the ease of digital publishing, and uses that to obscure the contributions of many of the people he's feuded with towards the goals he claims to champion. </span><br /> <br /> He also hypocritically affirms that creating controversy and the attendant hate-speech that comes with online comments is necessary, while saying that Sarah Horrocks is being &quot;denied&quot; the ability to contribute to RPGs because she doesn't want to deal with... creating content that everyone apparently knew would generate hate speech towards her (because it's the Internet and nobody is surprised at the fact that a transwoman got attacked in comment sections for putting a transwoman in her game, even if it's despicable). Again, dodging any valid criticism to attack &quot;cishet dudes,&quot; but then demanding that anyone that attacks the Prelude work... be held to some sort of account regardless of how well informed their criticism is.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Zak agreed to behave, but not. Within all of 5 days, he was right back to, &quot;everyone that disagrees with me is a liar, and everything I've done to make the lives of those 'liars' hell is not only justified buy awesome.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:33:12-08:00","id":1060282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1060258#post1060258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait.................. what? Why did he do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The SAppelcline account was used on a number of places (mostly Reddit and Google+) to hype up Zak's products and denounce Zak's detractors; and was actually doing so for around a year (though people called him out on it pretty quickly, it wasn't until very recently that it was undeniably caught).<br /> <br /> So, there's two basic scenarios:<br /> <br /> Zak is lying and it was him the whole time, impersonating someone to hype his own shit.<br /> Zak is telling the truth and he let someone he knew was lying use his personal computer to perpetuate said lying via impersonation.<br /> <br /> In either case, makes Zak's blog post about how trolls prohibitively increase the cost of creativity as long as the cost of lying is low seem fairly damning on him, since he's all for enabling liars on his side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:37:56-08:00","id":1060285,"title":"","content":"Wow, just wow. So is he still under contract at white wolf for other projects or was he just hired for the mobile game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:38:48-08:00","id":1060286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1060282#post1060282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The SAppelcline account was used on a number of places (mostly Reddit and Google+) to hype up Zak's products and denounce Zak's detractors; and was actually doing so for around a year (though people called him out on it pretty quickly, it wasn't until very recently that it was undeniably caught).<br /> <br /> So, there's two basic scenarios:<br /> <br /> Zak is lying and it was him the whole time, impersonating someone to hype his own shit.<br /> Zak is telling the truth and he let someone he knew was lying use his personal computer to perpetuate said lying via impersonation.<br /> <br /> In either case, makes Zak's blog post about how trolls prohibitively increase the cost of creativity as long as the cost of lying is low seem fairly damning on him, since he's all for enabling liars on his side of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most recently, the SAppelcine account made a post in response to an accusation against Zak saying, &quot;I didn't,&quot; that was then deleted and reposted from Zak's personal account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T15:20:57-08:00","id":1060310,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Can we please drop the discussion of Zak S. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/documen