lassic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1059177#post1059177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have a bias against nWoD. It feels very... odd to me. Like I feel it's SUPPOSED to be the Majora's Mask to oWoD's Ocarina of Time, but it ends up feeling more like Faces of Evil <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...really? Not Wind Waker, or even Four Swords but the Philips CGI Faces of Evil?....*sadness*...<br /> <br /> (Deep breath)...anyways, if you have poor opinions of CofD that's all well and good. But, I would recommend giving the 2nd Edition material at least a quick look through before passing definitive judgment over the gamelines as a whole. Otherwise it would be like looking at 1st Edition WoD and using it as a whole to judge all editions and supplements afterwards. <br /> <br /> If you have already taken a look at 2nd Edition and have based your opinion off of that then please disregard the above paragraph. CofD isn't for everyone, as much as I'd like to argue the opposite.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: ...I didn't see the part where you acknowledged you might have had a personal bias against CofD, and instead just focused on the Faces of Evil comment. I apologize for that.<br /> - . -'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Golly! 03-10-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T02:10:23-08:00","id":1061174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050293-world-of-darkness-preludes?p=1061035#post1061035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...really? Not Wind Waker, or even Four Swords but the Philips CGI Faces of Evil?....*sadness*...<br /> <br /> (Deep breath)...anyways, if you have poor opinions of CofD that's all well and good. But, I would recommend giving the 2nd Edition material at least a quick look through before passing definitive judgment over the gamelines as a whole. Otherwise it would be like looking at 1st Edition WoD and using it as a whole to judge all editions and supplements afterwards.<br /> <br /> If you have already taken a look at 2nd Edition and have based your opinion off of that then please disregard the above paragraph. CofD isn't for everyone, as much as I'd like to argue the opposite.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: ...I didn't see the part where you acknowledged you might have had a personal bias against CofD, and instead just focused on the Faces of Evil comment. I apologize for that.<br /> - . -'</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry. In every case I can see what they're going for. I feel like it's supposed to feel like &quot;our world through a shattered mirror&quot; and it's supposed to be this awesome revision, a new take on the genre. But everything feels off, to me personally. The only thing I liked, the ONLY thing, after scouring through both versions of Requiem, was Mandrakes. Plant Ghouls! Why didn't anyone in the oWoD think of that?","si